{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448593-what-is-the-genre-of-your-vampire-games","id":1448593,"title":"What is the genre of your vampire games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-15T09:48:21-07:00","id":1448593,"title":"What is the genre of your vampire games?","content":"For me, they always come in these flavors:<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Punk </b>is when you're a penniless Brujah and his runaway Goth girl Tremere girlfriend of 12th and 13th generation respectively living in an abandoned hotel because the Ventrue Prince murdered your mortal families after you revealed you were vampires to them. You now plot to get your revenge but need, first, to be hired by the Primogen to go sabotage the art gallery of stuffed human corpses (faked of course <img src=\"https://www.rpgpub.com/styles/default/xenforo/smilies/Logan20/21.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>) displayed by their rivak.<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Horror </b>is when you are a Toreador Embraced by a mad old Elder as their concubine who has successfully staked them, leaving them to burn, only to discover that you actually are not the person you remember them to be. No, your memory of your past was erased and you must use your wits and charm to pretend to be the monster you were made to be while trying to discover if you had a past at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Urban Fantasy </b>is when your characters enter a strange and fascinating world of vampires, demons, werewolves, and magic living under the surface of the mortal world. The point is not horror but to appreciate the beauty, terror, and weirdness of the surreal. The World of Darkness as a whole tends to be invoked here. Marco the Malkavian is an occult investigator who follows clues only he can see to find missing girls stolen by Boogeymen, solve the passions of wraiths, and investigate the secret of Nod's mysteries.<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Punk Urban Fantasy Horror </b>is when you're named Bloodrage Stonecold, 7th generation Caitiff with Celerity, Daimonion, and Thaumaturgy armed with two silver plated pistols that shoot explosive rounds while wearing a bandolier of incendiary grenades. Plus, you have a katana that is also silver plated. You exist to hunt werewolves, Sabbat, and giant flesh monsters. You follow the Path of Badassitude that has the central tenets of &quot;Fuck this shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit, I pretend to do the first two primarily but always end up with Stonecold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T10:19:01-07:00","id":1448600,"title":"","content":"let's be real here 90% of games is a comedy because all involved are clowns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T11:06:13-07:00","id":1448602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448593-what-is-the-genre-of-your-vampire-games?p=1448600#post1448600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's be real here 90% of games is a comedy because all involved are clowns</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True, it can be comedy tinged with something, but black comedy is still comedy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T11:40:15-07:00","id":1448606,"title":"","content":"Presently? Political Thriller. Vampires are movers and shakers (and wannabe movers and shakers) competing over resources and most of the PCs are trying to do the same while the Dhampir PC with some assistance of the most humane vampire in the city is assembling the assets needed to burn the whole corrupt system down.<br /> <br /> Side-bar: the Dhampir PC is the only one still on the original campaign track. All the players had made some very high Humanity PCs so I turned the Court into almost universally low Humanity monsters in one form or another so they\u2019d be encouraged to oppose and try to overthrow them. Instead everyone but the Dhampir sold out for the goodies of playing along with the corrupt system and didn\u2019t much care that their humanity dropped to what they decided was actually a more playable level of 6-ish... especially since two of the PCs had the blush of health merit and one had early riser so it the mechanical effects of the lower levels were largely irrelevant in the ways they cared about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T11:58:12-07:00","id":1448609,"title":"","content":"Dark Urban Fantasy with elements of personal horror and gothic punk and horror that ultimately are black comedies because players,<br /> Historic Dark Fantasy with elements of personal horror and gothic punk and horror that ultimately are black comedies because players, if it's set in a historical time period.<br /> <br /> And I'm trying to work out how to spin a Malkavian specific game into Cosmic Horror, but haven't decided what I'm doing yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:14:30-07:00","id":1448623,"title":"","content":"My games are a highly specific sub-genre called: Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Larger genres and their influence are never entirely constant enough. They shift in and out of focus as the flow of the story reaches various beats.<br /> <br /> I found out, quite some time ago, to stop trying to force myself, my games, and the games I play in, into hitting some genre. Genres are vague for a reason, and generally only applicable after the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T16:43:07-07:00","id":1448634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448593-what-is-the-genre-of-your-vampire-games#post1448593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gothic Horror </b>is when you are a Toreador Embraced by a mad old Elder as their concubine who has successfully staked them, leaving them to burn</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice 1e callback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T19:07:30-07:00","id":1448647,"title":"","content":"My V20 Chronicle? EXTREMELY Urban Fantasy. Admittedly, this chronicle was also conceived as a mostly episodic chain of adventures/plot-arcs, which would cause the tone to depend heavily on the scenario. First Episode (<i>&quot;Blood in the Gutters&quot;</i>) was meant to be low-key and gritty---the Coterie was ordered to resolve a string of murders which had the police scrutinizing a popular rack/hunting ground too closely. Although even that ended with the players briefly communicating with a Wyrm Spirit. Second Episode (<i>&quot;A Dream of Red&quot;</i>) saw the Coterie stranded inside a sorcerer's astral <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demesne_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Demesne</a>---exploring a seemingly endless temple-spire; matching wits with djinn; freeing a Mummy's <i>ba</i>; and coming away with a magic greatsword for their trouble.<br /> <br /> I admit my V20 game is very, very weird (although I think <i>&quot;A Dream of Red&quot;</i> will be the high water-mark for a long time to come).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 05-17-2021, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T04:28:16-07:00","id":1448672,"title":"","content":"We almost exclusively play with the DAV20 Rules in various historic settings.<br /> <br /> Urban Fantasy might be the correct genre by your definition OP, although direct crossovers a far and few between in my chronicles but in the constraints of the Vampire Lore no holds are barred. Of course I take some creative freedom to make it fit a bit more seemlesly<br /> <br /> For example I did a Chronicle with the Bath Domain from DAV20 Companion and made some vague crossover with the arthurian legend. A ventrue elder named Lucius Artorius Castus (Arthur) rises from torpor and rallies his faithful cainite &quot;Knights&quot; and the local Lhiannan under the leadership of an Elder named Myrddin (basically a version of Merlin). They are branded heretics by the mythraic Cult and a threat to the domain. The players are thrown into the conflict. Maybe choosing sides. Maybe choosing no side. Their decision.<br /> <br /> My players tend to play very scolarly characters who like to explore every nook and cranny of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T06:01:04-07:00","id":1448678,"title":"","content":"I'd catagorize my games as Gothic Fantasy. I tend to use more historical, pre-industrial time periods for my games. My games tend to have a fair amount of darkness in them, but I don't do too much horror, and I tend to play up the fantasy element (so even in an otherwise pretty pure VtM game I'm still likely to introduce some of the other critters from the World of Darkness like a Mummy or a werespider or what have you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T21:22:41-07:00","id":1448750,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://www.rpgpub.com/attachments/wandas-jpg.30931/\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> My ideal WOD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T14:37:01-07:00","id":1448806,"title":"","content":"Crime Drama with a side of Everything Is Terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T14:45:23-07:00","id":1448807,"title":"","content":"Urban Fantasy with occasional dips into Gothic Punk Urban Fantasy Horror. Multisplat is the way i am doing it now, and i am having a good time as are my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T14:50:36-07:00","id":1448900,"title":"","content":"My setting is definitely Gothic Punk-- although Gothic <b><i>massively </i></b>predominates and the &quot;punk&quot; elements tend to be a little more gang-driven than traditional punk. My stories are very heavily political in terms of Camarilla politics. Even the parts of the stories that aren't political take place within the milieu of vampire politics, and players can never lose sight of the political ramifications of their actions.<br /> <br /> I suppose that would make my game something like 65% political intrigue thriller (with explosions of Bourne-like violence) and 35% novel of manners. <br /> <br /> In Phipps' terms, it's definitely more Gothic Horror with just a touch of Urban Fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T19:24:49-07:00","id":1448927,"title":"","content":"As far away from convention, genre, and trope as possible. I stick to one too reliably, my players start being able to predict my story beats, and if they become able to predict my story beats they can plan in advance and/or eventually get bored.<br /> <br /> If I have to turn a stomach-churning fomori encounter or a meeting with a methuselah into a Monty Python-esque non sequitur-laden comedy of errors, by god I will if it keeps my players on their toes.<br /> <br /> One of my more recent TC stories in The Before Times involved the PC's cooking up this scheme to infiltrate Mediasch with a Tzimisce fleshcrafted to look like Nova Arpad, to kill and replace her...along with a handful of other Anarch packs who had <i>the exact same idea and nobody thought to coordinate their efforts</i>. Meaning there were like six Nova Arpads running around Mediasch all trying to kill each other, none of which was the <i>actual</i> Nova Arpad.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well...I shouldn't say &quot;nobody&quot; thought to coordinate their efforts. None of <i>them</i> did. Nova Arpad, on the other hand, was <i>absolutely</i> happy to take up the job for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T07:13:42-07:00","id":1448980,"title":"","content":"I def favour Urban Fantasy, really eldritch stuff involving the Tal'Mahe'Ra and the Underworld or Superheroes with Fangs games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T08:38:19-07:00","id":1448991,"title":"","content":"I'm also quite fond of taking inspiration from the Film Noir themes, now that I think about it. Everybody is either morally muddled or dead. Murder, blackmail, corruption, whodunits, organised crime, betrayal, fancy suits, getting framed for somebody else's crimes, so on so forth... It's the usual vampire thing packaged with jazz clubs, flashbacks and the scent of cigarettes and rain<br /> <br /> Bonus points for a storyteller who keeps to the weird narration style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-19-2021, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:44:57-07:00","id":1449008,"title":"","content":"My game is similar in that regard. I don't know if I'd call it <i>gothic</i> but moral corruption is certainly a theme. There isn't a single NPC that isn't compromised in some way. Every character has at least one dirty secret, one betrayal they've worked or are working; not every NPC is an out and out villain (that'd get pretty dull) but they each have their dark side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T21:21:07-07:00","id":1449313,"title":"","content":"The Mood: Gothic. The world and its powers that be are large and imposing. Age, size, and power over people reinforces the protagonists' inherent weakness in the shadows of their oppressive looming and the greater schemes of the world. The alliance between the corporate and political classes, the bureaucracies and laws, pop culture and the mindless mob. All of them are against you. So is your past and your own personal failings. <br /> <br /> The Theme: Punk. Be yourself and fuck anyone who has a problem with that. You are a person and an individual rather than a number or a cog. You - yes, YOU - are important and your voice is worth being heard, provided you are willing to speak up and accept the potential consequences of not following the crowd. Ultimately, the only person who can save you is you. <br /> <br /> The Genre: Noir is the typical default. It's an often bleak setting rife with cynicism, fatalism, and moral ambiguity. You're a Protagonist, not a &quot;hero&quot;, and that's important. Your motivations are often inherently selfish, but odds are you're still more moral than the powers that be. Other people will try to use you for their own ends and vice versa. And this frequently results in a great deal of intrigue and tragedy. But also maybe the occasional well earned moments of triumph. <br /> <br /> This can easily veer into other areas such as Political Thriller, Heist, Mystery, Romance, Cosmic Horror, Splatterpunk, or violent Action.<br /> <br /> <br /> (In hindsight, I rather wish Vampire had done a series of sourcebooks about running the game in certain genres, including sample chronicles. Political Intrigue, Horror, and Romance would've been good ones. Maybe Action/War as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T06:54:14-07:00","id":1449338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448593-what-is-the-genre-of-your-vampire-games#post1448593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, they always come in these flavors:<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Punk </b>is when you're a penniless Brujah and his runaway Goth girl Tremere girlfriend of 12th and 13th generation respectively living in an abandoned hotel because the Ventrue Prince murdered your mortal families after you revealed you were vampires to them. You now plot to get your revenge but need, first, to be hired by the Primogen to go sabotage the art gallery of stuffed human corpses (faked of course <img src=\"https://www.rpgpub.com/styles/default/xenforo/smilies/Logan20/21.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>) displayed by their rivak.<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Horror </b>is when you are a Toreador Embraced by a mad old Elder as their concubine who has successfully staked them, leaving them to burn, only to discover that you actually are not the person you remember them to be. No, your memory of your past was erased and you must use your wits and charm to pretend to be the monster you were made to be while trying to discover if you had a past at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Urban Fantasy </b>is when your characters enter a strange and fascinating world of vampires, demons, werewolves, and magic living under the surface of the mortal world. The point is not horror but to appreciate the beauty, terror, and weirdness of the surreal. The World of Darkness as a whole tends to be invoked here. Marco the Malkavian is an occult investigator who follows clues only he can see to find missing girls stolen by Boogeymen, solve the passions of wraiths, and investigate the secret of Nod's mysteries.<br /> <br /> <b>Gothic Punk Urban Fantasy Horror </b>is when you're named Bloodrage Stonecold, 7th generation Caitiff with Celerity, Daimonion, and Thaumaturgy armed with two silver plated pistols that shoot explosive rounds while wearing a bandolier of incendiary grenades. Plus, you have a katana that is also silver plated. You exist to hunt werewolves, Sabbat, and giant flesh monsters. You follow the Path of Badassitude that has the central tenets of &quot;Fuck this shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit, I pretend to do the first two primarily but always end up with Stonecold.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty much the same way. First campaign I ran in the 90s, I had an idea of the local Primogen, what the politics were, and who the major players would be in the Chronicle. Everything was prepped for a game of intrigue, dramatic reveals, and general skullduggery as the characters simultaneously wrestled with their own bestial natures. Within five sessions, the entire coterie was riding around in a copy of the Munster family car that played the show's theme tune when it honked, followed in a clown car by three circus performer ghouls (a fire eater, a strongman, and an acrobat). Not what I'd originally had in mind, but we had fun all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}